## Salesforce documentation

A local index of the official Salesforce documentation is available through the `salesforce-docs` MCP server.

- Before writing or reviewing Apex, LWC, SOQL, Flow, metadata, API integrations or org configuration, use
  `search_salesforce_docs` to confirm API signatures, governor limits, release behaviour and required permissions.
  Do not rely on memory for limits or method signatures.
- Search with exact identifiers when you have them (class, method, component, field, error message) and use the
  `guide` filter to narrow (e.g. `apexcode`, `apexref`, `api_meta`, `api_tooling`, `object_reference`;
  `list_salesforce_guides` shows every name).
- When a hit looks relevant but incomplete, open it with `read_salesforce_doc` and read the surrounding sections.
- Cite the documentation URLs you relied on. If the docs don't cover something, say so, and say what you are
  assuming instead.
